  "name": "SECOND OPINION BONE MARROW ASPIRATE",
  "code": "1580",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>A <strong data-start=\"64\" data-end=\"88\">bone marrow aspirate</strong> is a diagnostic test used to evaluate the <strong data-start=\"131\" data-end=\"175\">composition, cellularity, and morphology</strong> of bone marrow cells. A <strong data-start=\"200\" data-end=\"218\">second opinion</strong> involves re-evaluating the original bone marrow slides and report to confirm or refine the diagnosis, especially when the initial findings are unclear or critical.</p>\n<p data-start=\"389\" data-end=\"446\"><strong data-start=\"393\" data-end=\"446\">Purpose of Second Opinion in Bone Marrow Aspirate</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"448\" data-end=\"790\">\n<li data-start=\"448\" data-end=\"536\">\n<p data-start=\"450\" data-end=\"536\">Confirm or rule out <strong data-start=\"470\" data-end=\"498\">hematologic malignancies</strong> (e.g., leukemia, lymphoma, myeloma)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"537\" data-end=\"634\">\n<p data-start=\"539\" data-end=\"634\">Clarify <strong data-start=\"547\" data-end=\"581\">non-malignant marrow disorders</strong> (e.g., aplastic anemia, myelodysplastic syndromes)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"635\" data-end=\"716\">\n<p data-start=\"637\" data-end=\"716\">Resolve discrepancies between <strong data-start=\"667\" data-end=\"714\">clinical findings and initial marrow report</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"717\" data-end=\"790\">\n<p data-start=\"719\" data-end=\"790\">Guide further treatment decisions, especially for complex or rare cases</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Finding</th>\n<th>Possible Interpretation</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Increased blasts (&gt;20%)</td>\n<td>Acute leukemia</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Dysplastic changes in &ge;2 lines</td>\n<td>Myelodysplastic syndrome (MDS)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Hypercellularity with fibrosis</td>\n<td>Myelofibrosis or other myeloproliferative neoplasm</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Increased plasma cells (&gt;10%)</td>\n<td>Multiple myeloma</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Numerous immature myeloid cells</td>\n<td>Chronic myeloid leukemia (CML)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Poor megakaryocytes</td>\n<td>Aplastic anemia or ITP</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Ring sideroblasts</td>\n<td>Sideroblastic anemia</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Granulomas</td>\n<td>Infections (e.g., tuberculosis), sarcoidosis</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"3444\" data-end=\"3463\"><strong data-start=\"3448\" data-end=\"3463\">Final Notes</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"3465\" data-end=\"3735\">\n<li data-start=\"3465\" data-end=\"3645\">\n<p data-start=\"3467\" data-end=\"3645\">The <strong data-start=\"3471\" data-end=\"3489\">second opinion</strong> should be interpreted in light of <strong data-start=\"3524\" data-end=\"3544\">clinical history</strong>, <strong data-start=\"3546\" data-end=\"3562\">CBC findings</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"3568\" data-end=\"3594\">additional lab results</strong> (flow cytometry, cytogenetics, molecular testing).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"3646\" data-end=\"3735\">\n<p data-start=\"3648\" data-end=\"3735\">Always correlate with <strong data-start=\"3670\" data-end=\"3692\">bone marrow biopsy</strong> if available for architectural assessment.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
